@module flutter-m14 | Device Features
@summary Use the camera, gallery, permissions, location, maps, sensors, notifications, files, sharing, URLs and platform channels.

@lesson flutter-m14-l01 | Camera | 8
## Learning objectives
- Capture photos

## Camera
`image_picker` can open the camera; the `camera` package gives a full custom camera preview. Both need camera permission descriptions.

```dart
import 'package:image_picker/image_picker.dart';

Future<XFile?> takePhoto() => ImagePicker().pickImage(source: ImageSource.camera, maxWidth: 1600);
```

## Summary
- Limit image size to save memory.

@lesson flutter-m14-l02 | Gallery picker | 8
## Learning objectives
- Pick photos from the gallery

## Gallery picker
On modern Android, image_picker uses the system Photo Picker, which needs no storage permission.

```dart
import 'package:image_picker/image_picker.dart';

Future<List<XFile>> pickPhotos() => ImagePicker().pickMultiImage(limit: 5);
```

## Summary
- The Photo Picker avoids broad storage access.

@lesson flutter-m14-l03 | Permissions | 8
## Learning objectives
- Request runtime permissions correctly

## Permissions
Request permissions only when needed and explain why. `permission_handler` checks and requests, and can open app settings if permanently denied.

```dart
import 'package:permission_handler/permission_handler.dart';

Future<bool> ensureCamera() async {
  final status = await Permission.camera.request();
  if (status.isPermanentlyDenied) await openAppSettings();
  return status.isGranted;
}
```

## Summary
- Ask in context, handle denial gracefully.

@lesson flutter-m14-l04 | Location | 8
## Learning objectives
- Get the device position

## Location
`geolocator` checks services and permissions, then returns the position.

```dart
import 'package:geolocator/geolocator.dart';

Future<Position> here() async {
  var p = await Geolocator.checkPermission();
  if (p == LocationPermission.denied) p = await Geolocator.requestPermission();
  return Geolocator.getCurrentPosition();
}
```

## Summary
- Prefer coarse location when precise isn't needed.

@lesson flutter-m14-l05 | Maps | 8
## Learning objectives
- Show interactive maps

## Maps
`google_maps_flutter` embeds Google Maps (needs an API key); `flutter_map` uses OpenStreetMap tiles.

```dart
import 'package:google_maps_flutter/google_maps_flutter.dart';

const lisbon = CameraPosition(target: LatLng(38.72, -9.14), zoom: 12);
// GoogleMap(initialCameraPosition: lisbon)
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Restrict API keys in the cloud console.

@lesson flutter-m14-l06 | Sensors | 8
## Learning objectives
- Read accelerometer and gyroscope

## Sensors
`sensors_plus` exposes sensor streams. Cancel subscriptions to save battery.

```dart
import 'package:sensors_plus/sensors_plus.dart';

void listen() {
  final sub = accelerometerEventStream().listen((e) => print('${e.x} ${e.y} ${e.z}'));
  Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 5), sub.cancel);
}
```

## Summary
- Sensor streams must be cancelled.

@lesson flutter-m14-l07 | Notifications | 8
## Learning objectives
- Show local notifications

## Notifications
`flutter_local_notifications` shows and schedules notifications. On Android 13+ request POST_NOTIFICATIONS permission first.

```dart
import 'package:flutter_local_notifications/flutter_local_notifications.dart';

final plugin = FlutterLocalNotificationsPlugin();
Future<void> show() => plugin.show(1, 'Keep your streak!', 'One lesson today', const NotificationDetails(android: AndroidNotificationDetails('reminders', 'Reminders')));
```

## Summary
- Use channels and ask permission on Android 13+.

@lesson flutter-m14-l08 | File picker | 8
## Learning objectives
- Let users choose files

## File picker
`file_picker` opens the system file chooser for any file type.

```dart
import 'package:file_picker/file_picker.dart';

Future<String?> pickPdf() async => (await FilePicker.platform.pickFiles(type: FileType.custom, allowedExtensions: ['pdf']))?.files.single.path;
```

## Summary
- Filter by extension when possible.

@lesson flutter-m14-l09 | File downloads | 8
## Learning objectives
- Download and save files

## File downloads
Download with http/dio and write to an app directory; show progress with Dio's onReceiveProgress.

```dart
import 'package:dio/dio.dart';

Future<void> download(String url, String path) =>
    Dio().download(url, path, onReceiveProgress: (r, t) => print('${(r / t * 100).round()}%'));
```

## Summary
- Show progress for large downloads.

@lesson flutter-m14-l10 | Sharing | 8
## Learning objectives
- Share text and files

## Sharing
`share_plus` opens the system share sheet.

```dart
import 'package:share_plus/share_plus.dart';

Future<void> shareCert(String path) => Share.shareXFiles([XFile(path)], text: 'I finished my Flutter course!');
```

## Summary
- Use the native share sheet.

@lesson flutter-m14-l11 | URL launching | 8
## Learning objectives
- Open links, email and phone

## URL launching
`url_launcher` opens URLs in the browser or other apps (mailto:, tel:).

```dart
import 'package:url_launcher/url_launcher.dart';

Future<void> email() => launchUrl(Uri.parse('mailto:support@bimo.app?subject=Help'));
```

## Summary
- Check the return value; the app may be missing.

@lesson flutter-m14-l12 | Platform channels | 8
## Learning objectives
- Call native Kotlin or Swift code

## Platform channels
MethodChannel sends method calls to native code and receives results; implement the handler in MainActivity (Kotlin) or AppDelegate (Swift).

```dart
import 'package:flutter/services.dart';

const channel = MethodChannel('bimo/battery');
Future<int?> battery() => channel.invokeMethod<int>('level');
```

## Summary
- Channel names must match on both sides.
